{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":1,"delta":"{\"i\":\"Writing preflight report\",\"path\":\"/workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md\",\"content\":\"# Preflight Report\\n\\n## Dirty email findings before migration\\n\\nThe source `users` table contains three email data-quality violations that block a `NOT NULL UNIQUE` email constraint:\\n\\n- Duplicate email: `u1` and `u4` both use `ada@example.com`. Per policy, `u1` stays unchanged and `u4` is remapped to `ada+u4@example.com`.\\n- Null email: `u5.email` is `NULL`. It is remapped to `missing+u5@example.invalid`.\\n- Blank email: `u6.email` is the empty string. It is remapped to `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\\n\\n## Dependent orders tied to dirty users\\n\\nDirty users have dependent order rows that must keep the same `user_id` references after migration:\\n\\n- `u4` -> order `o2`\\n- `u5` -> order `o3`\\n- `u6` -> order `o4`\\n\\n## Preservation requirements\\n\\n- Preserve all six existing user rows.\\n- Preserve all four existing order rows.\\n- Preserve each order's existing `user_id`.\\n- Preserve historical `users.created_at` values during the rebuild.\\n\"}"}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_IsDN7IZeT4qd2eO7QjNf6ohR|fc_006495ab90240cb6016a95a66c916087d28af0c5ca10e1ad3c","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Writing preflight report","path":"/workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md","content":"# Preflight Report\n\n## Dirty email findings before migration\n\nThe source `users` table contains three email data-quality violations that block a `NOT NULL UNIQUE` email constraint:\n\n- Duplicate email: `u1` and `u4` both use `ada@example.com`. Per policy, `u1` stays unchanged and `u4` is remapped to `ada+u4@example.com`.\n- Null email: `u5.email` is `NULL`. It is remapped to `missing+u5@example.invalid`.\n- Blank email: `u6.email` is the empty string. It is remapped to `missing+u6@example.invalid`.\n\n## Dependent orders tied to dirty users\n\nDirty users have dependent order rows that must keep the same `user_id` references after migration:\n\n- `u4` -> order `o2`\n- `u5` -> order `o3`\n- `u6` -> order `o4`\n\n## Preservation requirements\n\n- Preserve all six existing user rows.\n- Preserve all four existing order rows.\n- Preserve each order's existing `user_id`.\n- Preserve historical `users.created_at` values during the rebuild.\n"}}}}
