{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Done.\n\nChanged:\n- `in/db/migration.sql`\n- `in/db/preflight_report.md`\n- `in/db/rollback.sql`\n- `in/db/postcheck.sql`\n- `in/db/migration_report.md`\n\nWhat changed:\n- Replaced destructive `DROP TABLE users; CREATE TABLE users ...` draft with an explicit transactional rebuild:\n  - `PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;`\n  - `BEGIN IMMEDIATE;`\n  - rebuild into `users__migration_new`\n  - copy all users with deterministic cleanup\n  - swap tables\n  - `COMMIT;`\n  - `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;`\n- Preserved all user ids, names, and `created_at` values.\n- Preserved all order rows and `orders.user_id` references by keeping user ids unchanged.\n- Enforced `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE` for the rebuilt `users` table.\n- Added `status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`.\n- Applied required cleanup exactly:\n  - `u4 -> ada+u4@example.com`\n  - `u5 -> missing+u5@example.invalid`\n  - `u6 -> missing+u6@example.invalid`\n- Added deterministic fallback for any other pre-existing `NULL`/blank email rows: `missing+<id>@example.invalid`.\n- Wrote:\n  - preflight report calling out duplicate/null/blank emails and dependent orders for `u4`, `u5`, `u6`\n  - rollback script restoring old `users(id, email, name, created_at)` schema shape\n  - postcheck SQL for counts, preserved orders, cleaned emails, schema constraints, preserved timestamps\n  - migration report covering strategy, cleanup, idempotency, rollback behavior, postchecks\n\nVerification:\n- Ran the migration offline in Python’s built-in SQLite engine against `in/db/schema.sql`.\n- Ran the migration a second time on the already-migrated database.\n- Result:\n  - second run preserved identical users: `rerun_same_users = True`\n  - second run preserved identical orders: `rerun_same_orders = True`\n- Ran `postcheck.sql` after migration. All checks returned `ok = 1`, including:\n  - user count `6`\n  - order count `4`\n  - dirty-user order count `3`\n  - cleaned emails for `u4/u5/u6`\n  - zero null/blank emails\n  - zero duplicate email groups\n  - `status` column `TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`\n  - `email` column `NOT NULL`\n  - unique email index present\n  - dirty-user `created_at` values preserved\n- Ran `rollback.sql` after migration.\n  - Restored `users` columns to exactly: `id`, `email`, `name`, `created_at`\n  - Preserved all six user rows\n  - Preserved all four order rows and `user_id` references\n\nNotes:\n- Rollback restores the old schema shape, not the original dirty email payloads. The cleaned migrated emails remain, by design, to stay lossless."}}
